  "question": {
    "text": "<p>As shown in the figure, a potentiometer wire of resistance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math> and length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> is connected with resistance box (R.B.) and a standard cell of emf <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>. For a resistance &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&#39; of resistance box introduced into the circuit, the null point for a cell of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mV</mi></math> is found to be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. The value of &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&#39; is&nbsp;_____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/d4323323-403e-4e0a-a7bc-938379eab464-image.png\" style=\"width: 150px; height: 152px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "780",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given here,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#949;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>.</p><p>Using the relation,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>, we have</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>60</mn><mn>300</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>780</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math></p></blockquote>",
